+**libSQL vector-index schema from `sqld` is not openable in Turso Database.**
+A SQLite-format file produced by libSQL server (`sqld`) or embedded libSQL that
+contains `CREATE INDEX ... ON ... (libsql_vector_idx(...))`, together with the
+associated `libsql_vector_meta_shadow` and `<index>_shadow` objects, remains
+readable by stock SQLite for the application table and vector blob columns, but
+`PRAGMA integrity_check` and `.dump` reimport fail in stock SQLite because
+`libsql_vector_idx()` is unknown there. Turso Database refuses to open the
+whole file with `invalid expression in CREATE INDEX: libsql_vector_idx (...)`.
+This is a cross-engine schema-portability gap, not evidence of data corruption.
+The vector values themselves stay ordinary portable blobs. Removing the vector
+index and its shadow objects restores a conventional SQLite file. Managed Turso
+Cloud behaviour was not tested here. Reproduction:
+[`withnative/libsql-vector-portability-evidence`](https://github.com/withnative/libsql-vector-portability-evidence).
+
+**Expression indexes must use Turso-supported expressions.** Turso supports
+`CREATE INDEX ... ON table(expression)` for expressions it can compile, but
+does not recognise libSQL-only marker functions such as `libsql_vector_idx()`.
+See [Turso issue #3987](https://github.com/tursodatabase/turso/issues/3987).
+
